Blue Origin will test new Glenn upper stages

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.200
at NASA's Stennis Space Center.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.440
The company is also rebuilding its Cape Canaveral launch site.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.840
Parallel progress on the vehicle

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.720
and ground infrastructure supports future flights.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.980
Observer's note schedule pressure on the company.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.680
The work aims to meet target dates set internally.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.100
Relativity space expansion plans surfaced

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.360
in the latest space industry newsletter.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.500
On-going starship activity appears alongside those plans.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.400
The company continues to develop its Terran R vehicle.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.420
Associated manufacturing capacity forms part of the effort.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.600
Details remain limited to high-level announcements at this stage.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.080
Off-grid data center proposals face new scrutiny.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.380
The proposal's concern whether they can truly bypass grid constraints

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.700
at the scale AI training requires.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.620
Reports indicate power demand growth

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.640
continues to outpace isolated site solutions.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.880
Several firms are now revisiting hybrid grid plus on-site designs.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.000
The scrutiny follows sustained increases in overall demand.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:47.700
Ethiotelecom highlighted local AI talent during the cursor Ethiopia hackathon.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.700
Participants used the platform to build agent-based tools

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.300
under real-world constraints.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.480
The event drew attention to developer communities

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.400
outside traditional tech hubs.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.700
The hackathon focused on practical applications.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.340
Local involvement received emphasis through the event.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:11.380
A European launch startup is seeking $300 million at a $2 billion valuation.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.280
The round would fund further development of a reusable small-launch vehicle.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.420
Financial Times reporting covers the effort.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.440
Investors are watching how the valuation compares

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.340
with recent SpaceX adjacent funding activity.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.240
The sought-amount ties directly to vehicle development goals.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:33.760
One thing worth watching is that Russia's state program now projects

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:38.000
its first reusable orbital rocket no earlier than 2030.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.120
The timeline leaves a multi-year gap behind current Falcon 9

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.860
and Starship reuse rates.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.060
Closing that gap would require sustained funding

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.620
and engine test cadence that have not yet materialized in public reporting.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.160
On the AI front, cursor's agent swarm test

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.300
showed that rooting most coding work to cheaper models

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.160
after frontier model planning

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.760
can cut inference costs by more than 95% while preserving output quality.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.980
The result points to a practical way to scale developer workloads

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:11.880
without proportional spend growth.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:16.020
The benchmark isolated the planner's single expensive pass

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.860
from the much larger volume of execution tokens.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:25.200
XAI's Memphis campus continues to draw local tax revenue and administrative attention

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.700
as construction proceeds on additional compute capacity.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.200
Officials are now discussing allocation of those funds

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.180
alongside project milestones.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:38.260
The site forms part of the broader colossus class build out

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.620
that supports GROC training and inference.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.580
Quack AI's Q402 model is now selectable inside cursor for agent workflows.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.600
The addition gives developers an on-platform option

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.500
that pairs with existing planner execution rooting

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.120
without external configuration.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.560
From an engineering standpoint,

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:02.840
the cursor agent swarm approach rests on a simple economic split

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.320
where one high capability model generates the plan

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.580
while multiple lower cost models execute the steps.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.240
In raw terms, the planner still consumes the expensive frontier tokens.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.480
Yet the execution layer now runs on models

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.800
whose per token price is a small fraction of the planners.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.200
That division collapses the idiot index of the overall workflow

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.600
because the bulk of the token volume no longer pays the frontier premium.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:39.220
The measured drop from $9,373 to $411 for the same SQLT task shows the gap is not theoretical.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.960
Most of the original cost came from rooting every subtask through the expensive model.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.380
Once the planner hands off concrete instructions,

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.920
cheaper models can finish the work without measurable quality loss in this benchmark.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:57.200
The remaining cost is dominated by the planner's single pass

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.700
plus the lightweight verification steps that still use higher grade inference.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.540
What changes next is utilization.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.060
If the same pattern holds across larger code bases,

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.320
inference clusters can keep a small number of frontier GPUs busy on planning

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.980
while the majority of the fleet runs cheaper models at higher throughput.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.400
That rebalancing directly improves the economics of serving developer traffic at scale

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.880
and reduces the power and interconnect demand that would otherwise grow linearly with every added

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:33.960
user. The architecture also creates a clearer separation between the scarce resource of frontier

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:40.180
planning capacity and the abundant resource of execution tokens, allowing operators to size

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.840
clusters around actual token economics rather than uniform model pricing.

